   },
   "roundness": null,
   "text": "Settled: TRIAGE is a branch inside ONE function, not a fork between two. The routes diverge\nat grounding (4), stay apart through output (6), and rejoin at acceptance (7) \u2014 shared\nmachinery, route-specific checklist. Both hand off to the same place.\n\nTwo things this stage still owes: the route-specific acceptance checklists are named but not\nwritten, and neither document has a declared home or naming rule \u2014 that is blocked on the\ncross-cutting \"Where the work is written down\", which is still drafted and unagreed.",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 5,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "originalText": "Settled: TRIAGE is a branch inside ONE function, not a fork between two. The routes diverge\nat grounding (4), stay apart through output (6), and rejoin at acceptance (7) \u2014 shared\nmachinery, route-specific checklist. Both hand off to the same place.\n\nTwo things this stage still owes: the route-specific acceptance checklists are named but not\nwritten, and neither document has a declared home or naming rule \u2014 that is blocked on the\ncross-cutting \"Where the work is written down\", which is still drafted and unagreed.",
